<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joshua Nkomo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1917–1999</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joshua Nkomo was a Zimbabwean nationalist who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe-african-peoples-union">Zimbabwe African People's Union</a> (ZAPU) in 1961 and led it through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war against white minority rule in Rhodesia. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-mugabe">Robert Mugabe</a> he formed the Patriotic Front in 1976. After independence he was driven from government in 1982 amid the Gukurahundi repression in Matabeleland, but ZAPU merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanu-pf">ZANU-PF</a> in 1987 and he became vice-president in 1990.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joshua-nkomo.jpg" alt="Joshua Nkomo" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rob Croes for Anefo · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joshua_Nkomo_(1978).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
